If 200 candidates already exist in the wordlist, those
existing candidates are skipped.


------------------------------------------------------------
8. TRAVERSAL STRATEGY
------------------------------------------------------------

Traversal strategy controls the ORDER in which PASSGEN
explores possible combinations.

It does NOT mean that one strategy creates different
possible combinations from another when the search space is
the same.

The difference is primarily the order in which candidates
are visited.


------------------------------------------------------------
9. SEQUENTIAL
------------------------------------------------------------

Sequential means:

"Go through the combinations in normal systematic order."

Example alphabet:

a,b,c

