ab
ac
ba
bb
bc
ca
cb
cc

Use this when you want a predictable and straightforward
search order.


------------------------------------------------------------
10. ALPHABETICAL
------------------------------------------------------------

Alphabetical means PASSGEN sorts the available alphabet
before traversing it.

Example:

Input:

q,w,e,r

Alphabetical ordering becomes:

e,q,r,w

The generator then explores combinations according to that
ordering.

Use this when you want a predictable alphabetically ordered
search.


------------------------------------------------------------
11. RANDOM
------------------------------------------------------------

Random means PASSGEN chooses combinations in a randomized
order instead of starting from the beginning and moving
straight through the search space.

Example:

Instead of:

